# What NOT to publish when the patient portal is deployed.
#
# This directory is its own Vercel project, so `vercel` run from here uploads
# THIS tree — not the repo root. The same rule as the root .vercelignore
# applies: the deployed site is a public URL, so anything here that is not
# part of the portal itself would be browsable by whoever gets the link.

# Local environment files. `vercel link` writes .env.local with an OIDC token
# into this folder, and this command uploads the working tree rather than the
# commit — so being gitignored is not on its own enough to keep it off a
# public URL.
.env
.env.*

# Build notes for whoever picks the prototype up, not for the people it is
# being shown to.
README.md
